Add a cargo-fuzz target `ndjson` (upstream has none)

A lean4export NDJSON stream checked as the arena runs kefir (and kefir-wasm)
with --axiom-policy=allow-all-declared-axioms: one single-use Run, checking
on the calling thread (wasm32 has no threads), the report written to a sink.
The Run, which reserves its report buffers before reading input, is built
once from a static constructor; each input takes the one in wasmfuzz's
snapshot, other runners build a fresh one after the first input.
Upstream: none (no fuzz targets upstream, checked 2026-11-22).

